# setuptools' sdist defaults sweep in tests/test*.py, but not tests/conftest.py
# and not examples/. That shipped a suite that was both unguarded (conftest is
# what stops a test run from POSTing to the real backend) and partly vacuous
# (the notebook checks globbed an examples/ directory that wasn't there, so they
# passed without testing anything). A half-suite is worse than none; the tests
# live in the repo.
prune tests
